Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day: a month flipped. By
4 October the desk had **412 reports**.

**Merged as one issue.** The parser reads dates month first, and our tenants write the day
first. The fix is queued.

<Callout>
Known. One issue, one fix queued.
</Callout>

<Callout kind="warn">
Three problems, not one. <b>This supersedes the line above</b>, which is what the desk believed
while the reports were only ever read by their subject lines. The reports merged here describe a
parser that reads every date month
first, a <code>booking-v3</code> date hint that disagrees with how the form stores the date, and
invites that land one day out. This ticket is the parser one, and fixing the parser leaves the
other two open. One of them was in the wrong ticket: the 33 reports of the date-hint cause are
merged into <a href="https://github.com/BlackShaira/kurs/issues/2">#2</a> now, which is why the
table below shows one cause and not two. The one-day reports stay counted here and footnoted,
which is where this kb files them. Read
<a href="/kb/incidents/4471/split">what this ticket actually holds</a>, with the counts built
from the data.
</Callout>

